    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n13457" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dēstĭtūtĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		destituo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a forsaking, deserting; deceiving, a failure,
				disappointment</i> (very rare), Cin. Clu. 26, 71;
					<i><span class="en">id. Quint. 5, 20</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Suet.
				Dom. 14</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A putting away, abandoning</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">peccati,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Heb. 9, 26</span></i>
			.</div>
